["I need to make 24 using 10, 1, 2, 6 with each number once.\n\nLet me try combinations:\n- 10 + 1 + 2 + 6 = 19, no\n- 10 * 2 + 6 - 1 = 25, no\n- 10 * 2 - 6 + 1 = 15, no\n- 10 * 2 - 6 * 1 = 14, no\n- 10 + 6 * 2 + 1 = 23, no\n- 10 + 6 * 2 - 1 = 21, no\n- 6 * 2 * 1 + 10 = 22, no\n- 6 * (10 - 2) * 1 = 48, no\n- 6 * (10 - 2) / 1 = 48, no\n- (10 - 6) * 2 * 1 = 8, no\n- (10 - 6) * (2 + 1) = 12, no\n- (10 + 2) * (6 - 1) = 60, no\n- (10 - 1) * 2 + 6 = 24! Let me check: 9 * 2 = 18, 18 + 6 = 24. Yes!\n\nWait, that uses 10, 1, 2, 6. Yes!\n\n(10 - 1) * 2 + 6 = 24.\n\nLet me verify: 10 - 1 = 9, 9 * 2 = 18, 18 + 6 = 24. Correct!\n"]